# GET /catalog/<entry>: one named label, its exact bytes and their sha256
route     GET /catalog/<entry>
handler   entry
memo      the contract of GET /catalog/<entry> on tiesapi.com
input
  <entry>: the name of a file under catalog/entries/ (letters, digits, _ . -, and / between parts)
processing
  1 refuse a name that is not in that form
  2 read the exact bytes of catalog/entries/<entry>
  3 hash them
output
  200 {entry, url, sha256, bytes}; 404 {error: "no such catalog entry"}
  check: sha256 of bytes equals sha256; the same file in git hashes the same
graph
  builds on catalog
example
  GET /catalog/sop-nonce-chain
